<title>SWEDEN: Skanska wins 210 mln Skr Iceland order.</title>
<headline>Skanska wins 210 mln Skr Iceland order.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-06-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish construction group Skanska said on Monday it won a 420 million crown ($54.1 million) order for an Icelandic hydro-electric power plant project along with Istak of Iceland and Phil &amp; Son of Denmark.</p>
<p>The order was placed by Iceland's national power utility Landsvirkjun and Skanska will get half of the order value, it said in a statement.</p>
<p>The new plant will have an installed output of 120 megawatts. Construction is due to be complete in January 2000, Skanska added.</p>
<p>&quot;It is very satisfying that we again succeeded in winning a hydropower project on Iceland, the fourth,&quot; said Skanska spokesman Per Hofvander in the statement.</p>
<p>-- Birgitta Forsberg, Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1017 ($ = 7.763 Swedish Crowns)</p>
